# 2. ABSOLUTE EXECUTION RULES

## 2.1 Repository Inspection Before Modification

Inspect the existing repository before proposing or implementing changes.

Do not assume that a class works merely because it exists.

Do not assume that a module is unused merely because it is not visible in the main UI.

Do not assume that an adapter performs real inference merely because it implements an inference interface.

Trace imports, object construction, dependency injection, runtime calls, data movement, and output consumption.

Every important conclusion must include:

- Exact repository-relative file path.
- Class, function, or exported symbol.
- Relevant line range where available.
- Actual caller or consumer.
- Execution status.
- Evidence supporting the conclusion.

## 2.2 No Premature Implementation

During this mission:

- Do not rewrite the ASR engine.
- Do not introduce a new ASR model.
- Do not change the audio renderer.
- Do not redesign the UI.
- Do not remove existing engines.
- Do not delete the Google GenAI dependency.
- Do not delete server routes before determining their consumers.
- Do not change package versions.
- Do not introduce new infrastructure packages.
- Do not replace existing abstractions with speculative alternatives.

You may add documentation and audit scripts when necessary.

If a critical security issue is discovered, document it and propose the smallest safe remediation. Do not silently expand the mission.

## 2.3 Evidence Classification

Every finding must be classified as one of:

- OBSERVED: directly verified in source code or execution.
- TESTED: demonstrated by an executed test.
- INFERRED: supported by multiple observations but not directly demonstrated.
- HYPOTHESIS: requires an experiment.
- UNKNOWN: insufficient evidence.

Never present an inference as an observed fact.

Never present a planned capability as an implemented capability.

Never present a passing TypeScript build as proof of runtime correctness.

